                <airSeal>At the time of the inspection we notice some air leakage on the following house components:

-Crawl space/basement (combustion air supply for previous heating system)

-Door (Kitchen)

During the walk through we notice a high level of air leakage coming from the basement. The old combustion air supply for the old oil furnace still in place and it?????????s not seal. We recommend to seal it.

</airSeal>
                <ceilings>The actual insulation level of your attic is R-30,  we recommend the addition of insulation to meet the city of Whitehorse standard of R-60. 

The addition of insulation will increase your capacity to retain heat into the living space and reduce heat loss during winter. In the summertime, the addition of insulation will slow down the migration of heat from the attic to the upper floor. 

</ceilings>
                <foundation>We recommend to increase the insulation level of your basement and crawl space floor. You are eligible for $2.50/square inch for the addition of R-20+,  and $ 3.50/square inch for R-30+.</foundation>
                <windows>At the time of the assessment we notice condensation inside the windows on some units. We recommend the replacement of the windows by Energy Star certified unit, and for Canada Zone 3.</windows>
                <doors>We recommend the replacement of the original doors for Energy Star certified units.  </doors>
                <VentilationSystem>The result of the infiltration test has shown that your house's natural air exchange is not enough. We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) HVI (Home Ventilation Institute) and Energy Star certified, to ensure proper ventilation inside your home.</VentilationSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
